<title>TUNISIA: Hyundai shortlisted for Tunisian contract.</title>
<headline>Hyundai shortlisted for Tunisian contract.</headline>
<dateline>TUNIS 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Korea's Hyundai Construction Co Ltd, and Spain's Ferrovial had been shortlisted to win a tender to build a sports stadium in Tunisia, sources close to the project said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The sources told Reuters the 60,000 seat stadium will be built in the &quot;7 November Sports City&quot; in Rades, south of Tunis, to host the Mediterranean Games in 2001.</p>
<p>The cost of the stadium was estimated at $120 to $130 million, they said.</p>
</text>
